            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0562" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15 Arms Truce/15: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-18T00:00:00+01:00">September 18,
                        1931—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received September 19—8:55
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>139. With reference to your 113, of September 18, 1 p.m. I have consulted
                    Drummond in strict confidence. It is his intention to suggest to the Chairman of
                    the Third Committee to propose that the Committee at its afternoon meeting today
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">tomorrow</hi>] urgently invite the non-League
                    states which sat on the Preparatory Commission to participate in the Third
                    Committee in the discussion of the Grandi proposal. These non-League states are
                    the United States, Russia, and Turkey. The Secretary-General is certain that the
                    proposal will at once be accepted by the Committee. He will have a written
                    invitation already prepared which he will hand to me and which I will at once
                    send to the Department. It is important to have your formal acceptance, together
                    with the designation, in time for delivery to Drummond on the morning of the
                    21st should developments follow along this line.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
